# No local models (frozen)

This rule is the **Cursor enforcement surface** for the repository-wide freeze
policy documented in `docs/LOCAL_MODELS_FROZEN.md`. The policy is not Cursor-
specific; local-model deviation must be recorded in the repo evidence, not
silently re-scoped to one tool.

Until the user explicitly says otherwise:

- **Do not** point kagent `ModelConfig` / agents at `agent-fast`, `agent-review`, or any `local-*` / Ollama model.
- **Do** use cloud-only LiteLLM alias `agent-coder` (DeepSeek) for live A2A, tool-loop, and smokes.
- **Do not** fall back to local models when cloud fails — record BLOCKED evidence instead.
- Config may still *describe* local backends; never invoke them.

See also: `docs/LOCAL_MODELS_FROZEN.md` (canonical policy) and LLMLite `docs/LOCAL_MODELS.md`.
